{"name":"Lemonade Stand","hex":"#f2ca3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemonade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flavored beverage consisting of water, lemon, and sweetener, sometimes ice, served mainly as a refreshment.","A clear, usually carbonated, beverage made from lemon or artificial lemon flavouring, water, and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemonade"},{"term":"stand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To position or be positioned physically:\n To support oneself on the feet in an erect position.","To support oneself on the feet in an erect position."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of standing.","A defensive position or effort."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemonade Stand","blocks":[{"text":"Lemonade Stand is a business simulation game created in 1973 by Bob Jamison of the Minnesota Educational Computing Consortium (MECC). In it, the player moves through several rounds of running a lemonade stand, beginning each round by making choices dependent on their current amount of money about their stock, prices, and advertising. In each round, the results are randomized based on the player's inputs, as well as affected by random events such as thunderstorms and street closures. Each round ends with a summary of the player's current status, and the game ends after 12 rounds."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade_Stand","wikidata":"Q6521381"},{"title":"Lemonade Stand (podcast)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemonade Stand is a business podcast that launched on March 6, 2025, hosted by content creators Brandon Ewing (Atrioc), Aiden McCaig (Calvin), and Douglas Wreden (DougDoug). The podcast discusses business, technology, and politics, targeting a primarily Generation Z audience. In October 2025, Vox Media announced a partnership with the podcast, assuming sales, marketing, and distribution responsibilities."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Lemonade_Stand_Podcast.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade_Stand_(podcast)","wikidata":"Q135209751"},{"title":"Lemonade stand","blocks":[{"text":"A lemonade stand is a business that is commonly owned and operated by children to sell lemonade. The concept has become an icon of youthful summertime North American culture. The term may also be used to refer to stands that sell similar beverages such as iced tea and soda. They are typically erected in the summer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/YOUNGSTER_MANS_A_ROADSIDE_STAND_SELLING_SQUASH%2C_CUCUMBERS_AND_LEMONADE_ON_SIMS_ROAD_AND_GEORGIA_HIGHWAY_356_AT..._-_NARA_-_557757.jpg/330px-YOUNGSTER_MANS_A_ROADSIDE_STAND_SELLING_SQUASH%2C_CUCUMBERS_AND_LEMONADE_ON_SIMS_ROAD_AND_GEORGIA_HIGHWAY_356_AT..._-_NARA_-_557757.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade_stand","wikidata":"Q3496544"},{"title":"Lemonade","blocks":[{"text":"Lemonade is a sweetened lemon-flavored drink that may be carbonated or un-carbonated; when carbonated, it is sometimes called a lemon soda. There are many varieties of lemonade found throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg/330px-Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade","wikidata":"Q893"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Lemonade_Stand_1.png/500px-Lemonade_Stand_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Lemonade_Stand_1.png/500px-Lemonade_Stand_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The decision-making screen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemonade_Stand_1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Lemonade_Stand_2.png/500px-Lemonade_Stand_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Lemonade_Stand_2.png/500px-Lemonade_Stand_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The report screen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemonade_Stand_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Atrioc_Lemonade_Stand_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Atrioc_Lemonade_Stand_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Atrioc_Lemonade_Stand_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Atrioc_Lemonade_Stand_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtrioc_Lemonade_Stand_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Phantom_2024_SSBM-_Calvin_vs_Rupert_%28Sheik_vs_Marth%29_-_Top_48_LR4_screenshot_01_%28Calvin_crop%29.png/330px-Phantom_2024_SSBM-_Calvin_vs_Rupert_%28Sheik_vs_Marth%29_-_Top_48_LR4_screenshot_01_%28Calvin_crop%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Phantom_2024_SSBM-_Calvin_vs_Rupert_%28Sheik_vs_Marth%29_-_Top_48_LR4_screenshot_01_%28Calvin_crop%29.png/330px-Phantom_2024_SSBM-_Calvin_vs_Rupert_%28Sheik_vs_Marth%29_-_Top_48_LR4_screenshot_01_%28Calvin_crop%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhantom_2024_SSBM-_Calvin_vs_Rupert_(Sheik_vs_Marth)_-_Top_48_LR4_screenshot_01_(Calvin_crop).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip